--- A function that answers nothing, whose last line calls another function that
--- answers nothing with an argument that can fail, does not build compiled.
---
--- Interpreted: prints `1` and `end` (exit 0).
--- Compiled: does not build:
---   error[E0308]: mismatched types --> src/main.rs:36:314
---   error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused what Crow
---   accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program (`crow run -i` runs it meanwhile)
---   (rustc: expected `()`, found `CrowResult<()>` — the call's propagation block is
---   wrapped in a second CrowResult { ok: true, value: … } at the function's end)
--- Expected: both modes run alike. With any line after `show[maybe[n]]` in `run`,
--- the program builds (see hex_dump-2.co for what both modes then do with the failure).

fn show[x]
    log[x]

fn maybe[n]
    if n gt 0
        return n
    return error['not positive']

fn run[n]
    show[maybe[n]]

run[1]
log['end']
